# stdlib/str.rvl (item 181) embeds literal control bytes (HT and a newline LF)
# inside backtick templates so str_char / str_tab / str_newline are pure revl.
# Pin it to verbatim bytes so no autocrlf / EOL normalization rewrites the LF to
# CRLF (which would make str_newline() a two-char string).
stdlib/str.rvl -text
